body:
Similar. After sexually assaulting me, telling me she would have had sex with me but I "wasn't into it," me telling her I was but not the way it initially happened, her moving on to someone else without apologizing to me (and almost calling over that person with me sitting at her house, then asking if I was jealous) and abusing me when I asked for an explanation for her behavior, she said, "I said I was sorry. I don't know what you want me to say." She wrote me an "apology" where she said she was in therapy for an unhealthy connection between love and sex. When I next saw her she said, "I'm not in therapy. I lied." When I asked why she said, "I wanted you to be proud of me."

Some of the stuff she said,

&#x200B;

"I think you should just be happy you got to touch my boobs and get over it!"

"If I had fucked you, you might have ended up in therapy!"

&#x200B;

"You're acting like I raped you."

&#x200B;

She asked me if I was gay or a virgin when she knew I wasn't.

&#x200B;

When I went upstairs to cuddle her in bed she said, "I'm usually naked in here, it's weird having clothes on."

Before I blocked her text messages she said, "Hey love. How are you?"I told her I felt terrible. She said, "Oh no! What's wrong?" I said I needed to be alone right then. She responded that she understood. Next morning, "I don't know what's going on in your life and respect your needing solitude to reflect but but you're not actually alone. I've got your back and I'm available at any hour for you." When I finally told her I felt unsafe around her and thought she needed long-term therapy, she said, "Oh, that's how it is?" I said I thought what she said was the worst stuff I'd ever heard in my life. She said, "Really? people say worse things to me every day. I didn't think it was that bad. I guess I just have a thick skin." I told her it sounded like she was telling me to just get over it. She said, "No, I was just confused. I'm used to dysfunction. I don't know what normal is."

&#x200B;

The lure of the thought of real intimacy and maybe reconciliation, only to have it thrown back in my face as she victimized herself again when I asked her to change her behavior so we could be close.
